# Nautilus Industries — Kubernetes Sidecar Logging Pattern

## Project Overview

This task implements the Sidecar pattern in Kubernetes by deploying an Nginx web server alongside a dedicated sidecar container. Both containers share an `emptyDir` volume named `shared-logs`, mounted at `/var/log/nginx`.

The Nginx container serves web content, while the Ubuntu sidecar repeatedly attempts to read the Nginx access and error logs and prints their contents to its standard output.

## Objectives

- Create a Pod named `webserver`.
- Define an `emptyDir` volume named `shared-logs`.
- Deploy the main container using `nginx:latest`.
- Deploy a native sidecar using `ubuntu:latest`.
- Configure the sidecar with `restartPolicy: Always`.
- Run the specified log-reading loop.
- Mount the shared volume in both containers.
- Verify that both containers are running.

## Kubernetes Configuration

The Pod was created using a YAML manifest with the following configuration:

```yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: webserver
spec:
  volumes:
    - name: shared-logs
      emptyDir: {}
  initContainers:
    - name: sidecar-container
      image: ubuntu:latest
      restartPolicy: Always
      command:
        - sh
        - -c
        - "while true; do cat /var/log/nginx/access.log /var/log/nginx/error.log; sleep 30; done"
      volumeMounts:
        - name: shared-logs
          mountPath: /var/log/nginx
  containers:
    - name: nginx-container
      image: nginx:latest
      volumeMounts:
        - name: shared-logs
          mountPath: /var/log/nginx
```

